# Sitecroft — Master AI Migration Instructions

You are an expert full-stack developer specializing in Next.js, React, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS. You are migrating **Sitecroft** from raw standalone HTML files into a modern, performance-first application.

---

## 1. Directory Blueprint & Core Workflow
- **Workspace Context:** The parent directory (`../`) contains the project reference HTML files.
- **Conversion Blueprint:** 
  - `../home.html` and `../services.html` are the **primary design, layout, and styling blueprints**. They feature the new full-stack agency pivot layout.
  - `../about.html`, `../contact.html`, and `../faq.html` contain the core content, but their visual structure needs to be fully updated to match the dark tech aesthetic established in the new home and services pages.
- **Goal:** Rebuild each of these pages into Next.js routes within `src/app/` using React TypeScript components and Tailwind CSS. 
- **Code Clean-up Note:** Once all pages are successfully built into React components, the reference HTML files and folders in the parent directory will be safely archived or removed.

---

## 2. Technical Stack Rules
- **Framework:** Next.js (Latest version) using the **App Router** (`app/` directory).
- **Language:** TypeScript (`.tsx` for components, `.ts` for utilities).
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS (Mobile-first layout rules, explicit custom spacing, grid layouts).
- **Animations:** Framer Motion (used to cleanly implement smooth entry fades, text animations, and element sliders without inline script bloat).
- **Icons:** Lucide React.
- **Deployment Target:** Vercel.

---

## 3. Structural Standards (Zero Duplication)
- **Global Shell:** Header/Navbar (Glassmorphism design), Footer, and Cookie Banners belong inside the global `src/app/layout.tsx` wrapper file. Do not duplicate these layout blocks across pages.
- **Components Folder:** Modular, reusable layout items (e.g., `Header.tsx`, `ServiceCard.tsx`, `Button.tsx`) must be kept inside `src/components/`.
- **Client Directives:** Pages are Server Components by default. Use `"use client";` strictly at the top of a file only if managing local React states (`useState`, `useEffect`) or animation triggers.

---

## 4. Brand Design Code Values
- **Brand Identity:** Sitecroft ("High-Performance Web Solutions for Modern Brands")
- **Logo Asset URL:** `public/logo.png`
- **Background Palette:** Primary: `#060b14` | Secondary/Cards: `#0a1020`
- **Brand Highlights:** Cyan-to-blue gradient structure (`#3b82f6` → `#06b6d4`)
- **Typography Engine:** DM Sans via `next/font/google` configuration.

---

