---

## 6. Coding Guardrails
- **TypeScript Handling:** Explicitly define typed objects or interfaces. Never fall back on `any`.
- **No Incomplete Snips:** Provide fully written code blocks ready to test or use. Avoid truncation and placeholders.
- **Ask to Verify:** If a feature scope or complex element behavior is unclear, stop and request clarification.
